Add some sort of highlight to player, NPM's treasures etc. when they are below
trees.  As is the tree foliage hides them thoroughly

Add a brief pause - maybe half a second - before an antagonist attacks upon
reaching the player.  So they see you, walk toward you, and have a "prepare to
attack" pause.  This should be configurable by creature type.  The slow attack
speed gives the player more time to swing at them.

Add distinct behaviours for different types of characters.  We already have
antagonists, could have fauna that tries to run away, passive characters, etc.
The current behaviour works well for aggressors though.

Allow player to adjust game scale on the fly.

Asset collection (tree cutting, mineral mining, etc.) - a new type of cave
generation would be good for that, it could contain fixed map elements that can
be mined


There should be a specific order of operations when the player clicks on a
given location and there are two actions possible.  For example, if there is
coinage under an aggressor, and I click where either action could be triggered,
attacking the aggressor should take priority.  I think the order should be
aggressors -> other creatures -> dropped goods -> interactive static items
(e.g. entrances, non-moving NPCs).  There might be more subsets to cut up
there.

Add spawn points on fixed maps.  Same as those in generated maps.

create a map editor that builds upon the game interface.
